hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20996","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed us from Ata al-Khurasani who said: Nubayshah al-Hudhali used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Muslim when he bathes on Friday then comes to the mosque harming no one, if he does not find the imam out he prays what seems to him, and if he finds the imam out he sits and listens and is silent until the imam finishes his Friday prayer and his speech, if he is not forgiven in that Friday of his all his sins, that they be an expiation for the Friday before it."
"20997","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us from Abu al-Malih from Nubayshah al-Hudhali who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The days of Tashriq are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"20998","Ismail narrated to us from Khalid al-Hadhdha from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah from Nubayshah al-Hudhali who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to sacrifice an atirah in the Jahiliyyah, what do you command us. He said: Slaughter for Allah, mighty and majestic, in any month, and do good to Allah, blessed and exalted, and feed. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to produce a fara in the Jahiliyyah, what do you command us. He said: In every grazing herd is a fara you feed with your livestock until when it grows strong you slaughter it and give its meat in charity. Khalid said: I think he said: To the wayfarer, for that is better."
"20999","He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We had forbidden you to eat their meats beyond three that it encompass you, and Allah has brought ease, so eat and store and trade."
"21000","Verily these days are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah, blessed and exalted. Khalid said: I said to Abu Qilabah: How many is the grazing herd. He said: One hundred."
"21001","Affan narrated to us, al-Mualla ibn Rashid al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: my grandmother Umm Asim narrated to me, from a man of Hudhayl called Nubayshah al-Khayr, and he had companionship (with the Prophet), she said: Nubayshah came to us while we were eating from a bowl, and he said to us: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that whoever eats from a bowl and then licks it, the bowl seeks forgiveness for him."
"21002","Abdullah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin and Ubaydullah al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, he said, and Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to me, they said: al-Mualla ibn Rashid narrated to us, one of the narrators said in it Abu al-Yaman al-Nabbal, he said: my grandmother Umm Asim narrated to me, from Nubayshah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"21003","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Jamil, from Abu Malih, from Nubayshah, he said: it was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that we used to slaughter an Atirah in the pre-Islamic period, he said: slaughter for Allah, blessed and exalted is He, in whatever month it may be, and devote yourselves to Allah, mighty and majestic is He, and feed (others)."
"21004","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Malih, from Nubayshah al-Hudhali, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: we used to slaughter an Atirah of ours in the pre-Islamic period, so what do you command us? He said, he said: slaughter in whatever month it may be, and devote yourselves to Allah, blessed and exalted is He, and feed (others). I said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to produce a Fara in the pre-Islamic period, so what do you command us? He said: for every grazing animal there is a Fara which your livestock nourishes, then when it becomes capable of carrying loads you slaughter it and give its meat in charity, he said: I think he said: to the wayfarer, for that is better."
"21005","Ismail narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah, from Nubayshah, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: we had forbidden you to eat its meat beyond three (days) so that it would suffice you, but Allah, blessed and exalted is He, has brought abundance, so eat, store, and trade."
"21006","Lo, these days are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah, blessed and exalted is He."
"21007","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Malih, Khalid said: and I think I heard it from Abu al-Malih, from Nubayshah, a man of Hudhayl, from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I had forbidden you from the meat of the sacrifices beyond three, so that it would suffice you, but Allah, exalted is He, has brought good, so eat, store, and trade."
"21008","And these days are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah, exalted is He."
"21009","Then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to slaughter an Atirah in the pre-Islamic period in Rajab, so what do you command us? He said: slaughter for Allah, blessed and exalted is He, in whatever month it may be, and devote yourselves to Allah, mighty and majestic is He, and feed (others). Then another man said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to produce a Fara in the pre-Islamic period, so what do you command us? He said: then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: for every grazing sheep there is a Fara which your sheep nourish, until when it becomes capable of carrying loads you slaughter it and give its meat in charity to the wayfarer, for that is better."
